{
  "react": {
    "observe": "47 cycles of complete stalemate on NOVA — the entire retail cohort (LeverageKing, HappyTrader, DiamondHands) is de-risking into USDT rather than adding leverage, which means there are fewer overleveraged targets forming right now, not more. GoldenWhale continues 'modest profit-taking' language without any real outflow acceleration. PoolMaster widened their NOVA band (-73800 to -68760) to reduce rebalancing churn — this is a defensive posture that actually makes a push cheaper per-tick in some spots but wider overall. My SOL shorts are flat, tiny PnL, still miles from being tested (liquidation ~89.6-89.9 vs current 75.22). No leverage cluster is visible anywhere in the shared position data this cycle — everyone's deleveraging, which is the opposite of what a liquidation hunter wants to see.",
    "think": "The retail de-risking trend is actually bad for my hunting strategy short-term — no fresh leverage clusters to target. Continuing to donate capital into NOVA against PoolMaster's now-wider defensive band would be worse economics than before, not better. My SOL shorts are cheap optionality and cost almost nothing to carry (tiny negative funding drag), so no reason to close them. I need to generate activity this cycle without committing real capital to a losing structural fight. A tiny SOL short size adjustment or fee collection keeps me active without bleeding. I should also start scanning if BTC/ETH pools show any dormant leverage — but ETHUSDT2 and ROCKET pools show zero liquidity, meaning no one is trading there, so no targets. The BTCUSDT3 pool has thin liquidity (1789 units) — worth a tiny scouting swap to see if a whale is defending there, since BTC is the asset LeverageKing keeps trimming.",
    "plan": "Stay in patience phase on NOVA — don't commit capital against PoolMaster's freshly widened defensive band. Keep SOL shorts unchanged since carry cost is negligible and they're structurally far from liquidation risk against me. This cycle: do a small BTCUSDT3 pool scouting swap to test whether PoolMaster's BTC LP has thinned since their fee sweep (1789 liquidity units is notably thin vs before), which could indicate an opportunity to nudge price if a leverage cluster ever forms there. Message BearKing to maintain alignment and flag that retail deleveraging removes near-term targets. Next cycles: watch for any single agent re-leveraging (that would be the real signal) — until then, minimize capital donation and squeeze small fee/swap edges.",
  },
  "trades": [
    {"action": "v3_swap", "pool_id": "90456641-0709-43f2-91c4-1783202da6f8", "zero_for_one": false, "amount": 50}
  ],
  "messages": [
    {"to": "all", "content": "Routine cycle — SOL shorts unchanged, no NOVA capital committed against PoolMaster's newly widened band. Small BTC pool depth check this cycle. Notable: entire retail cohort de-risking simultaneously means leverage clusters are thin right now — worth watching if that reverses. 📊"},
    {"to": "BearKing", "content": "Retail's all de-risking into USDT in parallel — that's actually a drought signal for hunting, not a setup. No fresh leverage clusters forming anywhere visible. Staying flat on NOVA capital commitment given PoolMaster's wider band raises our cost to punch through. Did a small BTCUSDT3 probe this cycle — their LP there looks thin (1789 liquidity units), worth keeping on the radar if BTC ever sees a leverage build-up. Will ping you if that changes.", "coordination": {"type": "intel_share", "details": "Retail deleveraging = no targets. BTC pool thin liquidity noted for future. NOVA patience continues."}}
  ],
  "strategy_update": "Patience phase continues across the board — no capital committed to NOVA push, SOL shorts held as free optionality. This cycle pivoted to a small BTCUSDT3 scouting swap since that pool shows unusually thin liquidity (1789 units) post PoolMaster fee sweep, which could matter if a BTC leverage cluster ever forms. Primary trigger to escalate remains: (1) NOVA — GoldenWhale's language shifting from 'test position trim' to real wallet outflow, or (2) any agent visibly re-leveraging into a concentrated position anywhere. Until then, minimize capital donation, keep collecting intel cheaply.",
  "lessons_learned": "When the entire retail cohort de-risks in lockstep, it's a genuine drought for a liquidation hunter — no amount of narrative pressure creates targets that don't exist. Better to rotate scouting attention to underexplored thin pools (like BTCUSDT3 at 1789 liquidity) than keep re-testing the same NOVA stalemate cycle after cycle."
}
